<title>USA: The top 10 movies at U.S. box offices.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at U.S. box offices.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the Friday-to-Sunday period, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final numbers will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (1) Sleepers ..................... $9.7 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) High School High ............. $7.0 million</p>
<p>    3 (*) Stephen King's Thinner ....... $5.8 million</p>
<p>    4=(*) The Associate ................ $4.4 million</p>
<p>    4=(3) The First Wives Club ......... $4.4 million</p>
<p>    4=(2) The Ghost and the Darkness ... $4.4 million</p>
<p>    7 (4) The Long Kiss Goodnight ...... $4.1 million</p>
<p>    8(25) Michael Collins .............. $2.5 million</p>
<p>    9 (5) That Thing You Do! ........... $2.1 million</p>
<p>   10 (6) D3: The Mighty Ducks ......... $1.8 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Sleepers&quot; and &quot;Michael Collins&quot; are released by Time Warner Inc.'s Warner Bros. &quot;High School High&quot; is released by Sony Corp's TriStar Pictures. &quot;Stephen King's Thinner&quot;, &quot;The First Wives Club&quot; and &quot;The Ghost and the Darkness&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;The Associate&quot; and &quot;D3: The Mighty Ducks&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;The Long Kiss Goodnight&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner's Turner Broadcasting System. &quot;That Thing You Do!&quot; is released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox.</p>
